{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Break off the golden rings</b> He chose gold and not silver, because it indicates the attribute of Justice, and its appearance is like the appearance of fire. And as they further said (Yoma 45a), \"the gold of Parvaim\" — that it resembles the blood of bulls. Therefore the House of Sacrifices was made entirely of gold, and likewise the altar of incense, and likewise the cherubim, and they expounded concerning them (Mekhilta Yitro 10:3) that if one made them of silver, they are like gods of silver and gods of gold. Also, the form of a calf in gold is more effective than in silver."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:19:26.897397814Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}